  "title": "The top of the whole algebra is the wrong layer; the knot keeps emergence without depth",
  "subject": "Whether every law that composes like cycles keeps the top layer of its selected spaces rigid",
  "conclusion": "A simple Mal'tsev law on five values containing Z4 composes like cycles and keeps knots in its top, so the statement fails as phrased; the rigid layer is the top of each point's own section, proved when the sections come from one chain ring. A law that composes like cycles thus keeps emergence only below the top of a two-layer abelian section, whereas the knot keeps it on two values in its only layer.",
